# Case 0.1: Setup of a new Windows 11 VM

##Objective

Set up a new Windows virtual machine to practice Help Desk, IT Support, and Desktop Support troubleshooting scenarios. This virtual machine is also intended to be used as a Lab for Cybersecurity scenarios.

## Lab Environment

- Host machine: Windows laptop
- Virtualization tool: VirtualBox
- Guest OS: Windows 11
- VM name: Windows-11
- Network mode: NAT
- RAM: 4 GB
- CPU: 2 cores
- Disk: 80 GB

## Setup Steps

1. Downloaded and installed VirtualBox. 
2. Downloaded the Windows 11 ISO.
3. Created a new virtual machine named Windows-11.
4. Assigned RAM, CPU, and virtual disk resources.
5. Installed Windows 11.
6. Renamed the computer to Win-Support-Lab.
7. Installed Windows updates.
8. Installed VirtualBox Guest Additions.
9. Configured NAT networking.
10. Created a clean baseline snapshot.

## Validation Done

- Windows boots successfully. Positive
- Internet connection works: verified using ipconfig, ping and nslookupcomands
- Windows Update runs correctly: Updates are downloading and installing smoothly.
- Guest Additions are installed: VirtualBox Guest Additions Drive created and installion program run. Reboot performed after installation. 
- Clipboard works between host and VM. Yes. Bidirectional
- Snapshot was created successfully. Yes

## Screenshots

- VM configuration
- Windows version
- Windows Update screen
- Network adapter settings
- Snapshot baseline

## Lessons Learned Done

This setup created a safe and controlled Windows environment where support scenarios can be tested, documented, and restored using snapshots.

